      "id": "The Control Room Process is not fully adhered to in all meetings in that the protection arrangements associated with the occupational safety risks are not discussed",
      "type": "ContributingFactor"
    },
    {
      "id": "The continued planning and implementation of Back-to-Back possessions has introduced practices that are non-compliant with prescribed instructions in the I\u00c9 Rule Book for fog signal protection",
      "type": "ContributingFactor"
    },
    {
      "id": "The consistent booking of pre-established possessions with regards to work, limits and duration has led to possession protection being arranged to coincide with these limits instead of an assessment taking place on a site by site basis",
      "type": "ContributingFactor"
    },
    {
      "id": "The Weekly Circular is currently ineffective for communicating actual works that are to be undertaken on a given day/night due to the current practices of booking and cancelling of possessions",
      "type": "ContributingFactor"
    },
    {
      "id": "Late alterations to possession arrangements are not always communicated to all relevant personnel",
      "type": "ContributingFactor"
    },
    {
      "id": "Recommendations regarding possession protection planning and Back-to-Back possessions have been closed out by the application of the Control Room Process without being suitably addressed",
      "type": "SystemicFactor"
